english_question:
As shown in the figure, the following statements are made: 
 (1) There are 6 line segments in the figure; 
 (2) AB + BC > AC, because "the shortest distance between two points is a straight line"; 
 (3) To nail a wooden strip on the wall, at least 2 nails are needed, because "two points determine a straight line"; 
 (4) The distance between points A and C in the figure is the length of line segment AC; 
 (5) There is exactly one line through point A that is perpendicular to line BD; 
 (6) Ray BD and ray DB are the same ray.
 The number of correct statements is ( ) .
A. 2
B. 3
C. 4
D. 5

The three views of a geometric body are shown in the figure. What is the volume of this geometric body (unit: cm³)?
A. π + \frac{\sqrt{3}}{3}
B. 2π + \frac{\sqrt{3}}{3}
C. 2π + \sqrt{3}
D. π + \sqrt{3}

In the figure, triangles \( \triangle ABC \) and \( \triangle AEF \) have the following properties: \( AB = AE \), \( BC = EF \), and \( \angle B = \angle E \). Line segment \( AB \) intersects \( EF \) at point D. The following conclusions are given: 
1. \( \angle AFC = \angle C \); 
2. \( DE = CF \); 
3. \( \triangle ADE \sim \triangle FDB \); 
4. \( \angle BFD = \angle CAF \). Which of the following conclusions are correct?

The three views of a certain geometric body and some data are shown in the figure. What is the volume of this geometric body? ( )
A. \frac{3}{2}
B. \sqrt{3}
C. ^2
